Package: aconteceR
Title: Find, Categorise and Add Local Events on a Map
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tulio", "Name", email = "you@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Vladimir", "Agafonkin", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Leaflet library in inst/www/vendor/leaflet"),
    person("CloudMade", role = "cph",
           comment = "Leaflet library in inst/www/vendor/leaflet")
    )
Description: A bilingual (Brazilian Portuguese and English) Shiny app to find
    events near you: it opens on the closest city, shows events on a map
    coloured by price or category, with clustering and a monthly calendar, and
    lets you search, import and add events. The map and calendar modules are
    generic, so other projects (for example a rent and buy price map) can
    reuse them. Places (bars, clubs, restaurants, venues) come from
    OpenStreetMap, with opening hours, vibes, an "open late" filter, a
    neighbourhood view, a night-out planner and "before and after" suggestions
    around events. The same interface also ships as a single standalone HTML
    file.
